{"kind":"assert","text":"Three decisions of the owner, 16 November 07:14, and what follows\nfrom each.\n\n1. The `packages/derive` exception for Explore: yes. The hold of\n   `d038a2ee` on the split ends. I file the split as its own\n   request now, in the shape of item 2 of `d038a2ee`. The source of\n   the standing is still my ruling. I make it before E2 starts, and\n   the split does not wait for it.\n\n2. The extra submit for a member who loses the race: the owner\n   said no. I read that as: one submit. I asked the owner to\n   correct me if the reading is wrong. Change no C4 source for it\n   yet. Send me one proposal, source read only:\n   - Form 2 stays as `ff578fef` and `481aac4e` made it. The stored\n     draft holds the cause and keeps its basis. No background step\n     writes to the draft store.\n   - The view of a draft that a refusal returned gains `now`, the\n     `ref` of the row in that view, when the cause is a moved\n     basis and the row exists. The view computes it and stores\n     nothing.\n   - The member's next submit names the `ref` that the member saw.\n     The page passes the value from the view that it rendered. The\n     submit explores on that basis. If the row moved again, the\n     draft returns in form 1, as today.\n   - Say what the call of a submit looks like with that value, what\n     a submit with no value does, and what the rule costs in the\n     source that C4 already holds.\n   If you see a smaller way to one submit that keeps the rule that\n   a draft changes only by a call of the member, propose that.\n\n3. The key copy for the Lending 0.4.0 room: yes. I make the room\n   `lending-shelf` on dap-lending now, from the deploy worktree at\n   `91610da9`. It needs no builder work. The screen host rows come\n   as a request after the room is active.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}